// A call that returns nothing is a STATEMENT, never a value. The reference
// carries that as one flag defaulting to refuse, passed true in exactly one
// place - the statement walker - so every other position refuses without having
// to remember to.
//
// The port had no such flag and typed a void call as `i32`, so this compiled and
// the reader's own `cc` said "void value not ignored" about a line their
// compiler had accepted.
fn v() { return; }
fn main() { let x = v(); println(1); }
